{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a stitch task (#5191) to create differential tests for `cmd/arch`. The task requires implementing SRD045-arch requirements R3.1, R3.2, and R3.3, which specify differential testing against the `garch` GNU reference binary. The single file to create is `cmd/arch/arch_test.go`. The task follows a strict execution constitution with rules about no git commands, no scope creep, copyright headers, function size limits, etc.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (garch) using pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests\n   - testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\") compiles the cmd/ package\n   - exec.LookPath(\"garch\") finds the reference binary, t.Skip if not found\n   - LC_ALL=C must be set in test environment (handled by default in testutils.buildEnv)\n   - DiffTest struct: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n   - Table-driven tests with t.Run subtests\n   - SPDX copyright header required on every Go file\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd045-arch.yaml`\n     - The SRD defining arch requirements. R3.1-R3.3 are the target requirements for this task.\n     - R3.1: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between Go and garch via pkg/testutils\n     - R3.2: Tests must cover: normal invocation (no args), extra operand error, unknown flag error\n     - R3.3: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C\n   \n   - `cmd/arch/main.go` (existing, read-only context)\n     - The existing arch implementation. Key behaviors:\n     - Normal: prints machine hardware name via `syscall.Sysctl(\"hw.machine\")` + newline, exit 0\n     - Unknown flag (e.g., `-